#. type: Content of: <sect1><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:12
#, xml-text
msgid "About Logical Volume Management (LVM)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:15
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"LVM manages disk drives.  It allows multiple drives and partitions to be "
"combined into larger <emphasis>volume groups</emphasis>, assists in making "
"backups through a <emphasis>snapshot</emphasis>, and allows for dynamic "
"volume resizing. It can also provide mirroring similar to a RAID 1 array."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:23
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"A complete discussion of LVM is beyond the scope of this introduction, but "
"basic concepts are presented below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:28
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To run any of the commands presented here, the <xref linkend='lvm2'/> "
"package must be installed.  All commands must be run as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:34
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Management of disks with lvm is accomplished using the following concepts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:39
#, xml-text
msgid "physical volumes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:42
#, xml-text
msgid "These are physical disks or partitions such as /dev/sda3 or /dev/sdb."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:49
#, xml-text
msgid "volume groups"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:52
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"These are named groups of physical volumes that can be manipulated by the "
"administrator.  The number of physical volumes that make up a volume group "
"is arbitrary.  Physical volumes can be dynamically added or removed from a "
"volume group."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:61
#, xml-text
msgid "logical volumes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:64
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Volume groups may be subdivided into logical volumes. Each logical volume "
"can then be individually formatted as if it were a regular Linux partition. "
"Logical volumes may be dynamically resized by the administrator according to"
" need."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:75
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To give a concrete example, suppose that you have two 2 TB disks. Also "
"suppose a really large amount of space is required for a very large "
"database, mounted on <filename class='directory'>/srv/mysql</filename>.  "
"This is what the initial set of partitions would look like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:81
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>Partition  Use    Size      Partition Type\n"
"/dev/sda1  /boot  100MB     83 (Linux)\n"
"/dev/sda2  /       10GB     83 (Linux)\n"
"/dev/sda3  swap     2GB     82 (Swap)\n"
"/dev/sda4  LVM    remainder 8e (LVM)\n"
"/dev/sdb1  swap     2GB     82 (Swap)\n"
"/dev/sdb2  LVM    remainder 8e (LVM)</literal>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:90
#, xml-text
msgid "First initialize the physical volumes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:93
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>pvcreate /dev/sda4 /dev/sdb2</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:97
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"A full disk can be used as part of a physical volume, but beware that the "
"<command>pvcreate</command> command will destroy any partition information "
"on that disk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:104
#, xml-text
msgid "Next create a volume group named lfs-lvm:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:107
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>vgcreate lfs-lvm /dev/sda4  /dev/sdb2</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:110
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The status of the volume group can be checked by running the command "
"<command>vgscan</command>. Now create the logical volumes.  Since there is "
"about 3900 GB available, leave about 900 GB free for expansion. Note that "
"the logical volume named <emphasis>mysql</emphasis> is larger than any "
"physical disk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:117
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>lvcreate --name mysql --size 2500G lfs-lvm\n"
"lvcreate --name home  --size  500G lfs-lvm</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:121
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Finally the logical volumes can be formatted and mounted.  In this example, "
"the jfs file system (<xref linkend='jfsutils'/>) is used for demonstration "
"purposes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:126
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkfs -t ext4 /dev/lfs-lvm/home\n"
"mkfs -t jfs  /dev/lfs-lvm/mysql\n"
"mount /dev/lfs-lvm/home /home\n"
"mkdir -p /srv/mysql\n"
"mount /dev/lfs-lvm/mysql /srv/mysql</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:133
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"It may be needed to activate those logical volumes, for them to appear in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/dev</filename>. They can all be activated at "
"the same time by issuing, as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:139
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>vgchange -a y</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:142
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The LFS boot scripts automatically make these logical volumes available to "
"the system in the <command>udev</command> script. Edit the "
"<filename>/etc/fstab</filename> file as required to automatically mount "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:149
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"A LVM logical volume can host a root filesystem, but requires the use of an "
"initramfs (initial RAM file system). The initramfs proposed in <xref "
"linkend=\"initramfs\"/> allows to pass the lvm volume in the "
"<parameter>root=</parameter> switch of the kernel command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:156
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If not using an initramfs, there is a race condition in <application> "
"systemd</application> preventing mounting logical volumes through "
"<filename>/etc/fstab</filename>. You must create a <quote>mount</quote> unit"
" (see <ulink role='man' url='&man;systemd.mount.5'>systemd.mount(5)</ulink>)"
" as in the following example, which mounts the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/home</filename> directory automatically at boot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:165
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/systemd/system/home.mount &lt;&lt; EOF\n"
"<literal>[Unit]\n"
"Description=Mount the lvm volume /dev/lfs-lvm/home to /home\n"
"\n"
"[Mount]\n"
"What=/dev/lfs-lvm/home\n"
"Where=/home\n"
"Type=ext4\n"
"Options=default\n"
"\n"
"[Install]\n"
"WantedBy=multi-user.target</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:181
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The name of the unit must be the name of the mount point with the `/' "
"character replaced by `-', omitting the leading one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:187
#, xml-text
msgid "Next the unit must be enabled with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:190
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>systemctl enable home.mount</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/postlfs/filesystems/aboutlvm.xml:193
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For more information about LVM, see the <ulink "
"url=\"https://tldp.org/HOWTO/LVM-HOWTO/\">LVM HOWTO</ulink> and the lvm man "
"pages. A good in-depth <ulink "
"url=\"https://access.redhat.com/documentation/en-"
"us/red_hat_enterprise_linux/7/html/logical_volume_manager_administration/index\">"
" guide</ulink> is available from RedHat<superscript>&reg;</superscript>, "
"although it makes sometimes reference to proprietary tools."
msgstr ""
